      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "605787df3643f440d41b86d5",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f2f6f47cb5f2349c1873556|full_name}: Not a minor annoyance when they do so 6 times a minute or more. In this case targeting the perpetrator would've been the purpose. To get them to stop their anti-social behaviour... \nSince it's the instance at large that decides over vote kicks, maybe the instance at large should be able to also vote for the initiator to get their vote-kicking privileges temporarily stripped. (Would still be anonymous). Or at least give players individually the ability to ignore them.\nAt the very least there ought to be a large cooldown, that way you wouldn't be able to be spam it as a a lone person.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
